PegResponsiveIrm::setPegOracle(address)
├── given caller is not the current owner
│   ├── when caller is a non-owner or the pending owner has not accepted ownership
│   │   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount(caller)
│   ├── it should prioritize authorization over zero-oracle validation and checkpointing
│   ├── it should leave oracle and the complete IRState unchanged
│   └── it should not call the market or emit events
└── given caller is the current owner
    ├── when newOracle is the zero address
    │   ├── it should revert with PegResponsiveIrmInvalidOracle
    │   ├── it should reject before checkpointing the market
    │   ├── it should leave oracle and the complete IRState unchanged
    │   └── it should not emit events
    └── when newOracle is non-zero
        ├── given market is not set
        │   ├── it should skip the market paused query
        │   └── it should skip market accrual
        ├── given market is set
        │   ├── it should query paused with the exact PAUSE_TYPE
        │   ├── when the paused query reverts or its return data cannot be decoded
        │   │   ├── it should bubble the failure
        │   │   ├── it should leave oracle and IRState unchanged
        │   │   └── it should not emit setter events
        │   ├── when paused returns true
        │   │   └── it should skip accrueInterest
        │   └── when paused returns false
        │       ├── when accrueInterest reverts
        │       │   ├── it should bubble the market revert
        │       │   ├── it should atomically roll back market and IRM effects
        │       │   └── it should not emit setter events
        │       └── when accrueInterest succeeds
        │           ├── it should call market.accrueInterest exactly once
        │           ├── if the market calls back into this IRM, that callback should observe the old oracle
        │           └── it should retain callback-driven IRState changes except for a later recovery reset
        ├── when newOracle equals the current non-zero oracle
        │   ├── it should still perform the applicable checkpoint
        │   ├── it should accept the no-op address replacement
        │   └── it should emit SetPegOracle(currentOracle, currentOracle)
        ├── when newOracle has no code or no declared getPrice implementation
        │   ├── it should accept and store the address without sampling it
        │   └── later reads should depend on whether the target reverts or returns valid, empty, or malformed ABI data
        ├── given the post-checkpoint recoveryStartedAt is zero
        │   ├── it should emit exactly SetPegOracle(oldOracle, newOracle) among setter events
        │   ├── it should store newOracle
        │   ├── it should not emit an additional StressStateUpdated or IRStateUpdated for recovery reset
        │   └── it should preserve the complete post-checkpoint IRState
        └── given the post-checkpoint recoveryStartedAt is non-zero
            ├── it should emit SetPegOracle(oldOracle, newOracle)
            ├── it should store newOracle
            ├── it should clear recoveryStartedAt
            ├── it should preserve post-checkpoint borrowRate, lastUpdate and stressMode
            ├── it should then emit StressStateUpdated(stressMode, 0, 0)
            └── it should then emit IRStateUpdated with the resulting state
